    },
    "repo": {
      "id": 606263592,
      "name": "beshoynabeih/odoo-dev",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev"
    },
    "payload": {
      "repository_id": 606263592,
      "push_id": 21933361390,
      "size": 6639,
      "distinct_size": 6639,
      "ref": "refs/heads/16.0",
      "head": "5839660037f7cc79ae72adc7399b9d07614646fe",
      "before": "1e0f36ac288a58c7621f4c0bd5b8092c60b95864",
      "commits": [
        {
          "sha": "8cef4b2bfd16225817d060d11436a8dd94fc90a6",
          "author": {
            "email": "otd@odoo.com",
            "name": "Djamel Touati"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] purchase: allow vendor to confirm that delivery will be on time\n\nSteps to reproduce the bug:\n- Go to contact and select azure interior:\n    - Sales & purchase tab:\n        - Enable “Receipt Reminder” 1 day\n\n- Create a purchase order:\n    - Select azure interior as vendor\n    - add any storable product\n    - Delivery ate: Tomorrow\n\n- Confirm the PO\n\n- Go to the Scheduled Actions: Purchase reminder\n- Run it Manually\n- Come back to the Dashbord > Emails\n- Select the email for Azure interior:\n    - Try to click on “YES”\n\nProblem:\nA traceback is triggered:\n`AttributeError: type object 'datetime.datetime' has no attribute 'from_string'`\n\nWhen the “YES” button is clicked, we retrieve the “confirmed_date”\nfrom the arguments as a string and then call the `confirm_reminder_mail`\nfunction (https://github.com/odoo/odoo/blob/181c7d82e30d0848bbac7f7d0188e81aced0af07/addons/purchase/controllers/portal.py#L117).\n\nThis date will be localized to the PO timezone using the\n`get_localized_date_planned` function: (https://github.com/odoo/odoo/blob/a0be5ea52aeff3520f8f1a92206a5aad38fdaa82/addons/purchase/models/purchase.py#L823).\n\nWe then get the timezone and use the `astimezone` function to transform\nthis date, but since it is in string format, an error is triggered.\n\nThis problem was introduced following this change:\n\nhttps://github.com/odoo/odoo/commit/a0be5ea52aeff3520f8f1a92206a5aad38fdaa82#diff-86168e4c37e9a7c1437998990c2aa4e1690d16605812f57a81172936377b9c50L823\n\nBefore this fix, the date could be either a Date or a string, which was\nalready incorrect!\n\nopw-4028362\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#172343\n\nX-original-commit: f021f8e3480163584427ffa8adc2bfa28e5df9c0\nSigned-off-by: Quentin Wolfs (quwo) <quwo@odoo.com>\nSigned-off-by: Djamel Touati (otd) <otd@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/8cef4b2bfd16225817d060d11436a8dd94fc90a6"
        },
        {
          "sha": "8efbceb7d5de238c25ed2e00382fd0df5f73a8e1",
          "author": {
            "email": "app@odoo.com",
            "name": "Pierre Paridans"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] web: make error formatting more resilient cross browsers\n\nBefore this commit, the error service attempted to adapt the\n`error.stack` format to match the one used by Chrome.\n\nBut even then, the error_service_tests (that compare exactly the\ntraceback) didn't pass on Firefox.\n\nSince version 125, even Chrome itself doesn't pass that test.\n\nThis commit adapts the stack formatting code to ensure the actual\nerror name is present and its message, but without trying to match a\n(too) specific format.\n\nAlso in this commit, the related tests are adapted to be a little less\nstrict (and more resilient), but stil ensuring the actual error name and\nmessage are present.\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#172330\n\nX-original-commit: cb363cdaf9c1d9a72b3bb2303d94c2a18005238f\nSigned-off-by: Aaron Bohy (aab) <aab@odoo.com>\nSigned-off-by: Pierre Paridans (app) <app@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/8efbceb7d5de238c25ed2e00382fd0df5f73a8e1"
        },
        {
          "sha": "8904e982605627d7b195fcb75f8899d535a0067c",
          "author": {
            "email": "srma@odoo.com",
            "name": "Maira Salazar (srma)"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] hr_expense: correct tour test\n\nThe tour for hr_expense was not up-to-date and was not being called via a Python test.\n\nThis commit corrects that by updating the tour, adding checks for the button 'Create\nReport' and creating a python test file which runs the the tour.\n\nPart of task-3981049\n\nPart-of: odoo/odoo#169396\nSigned-off-by: Olivier Colson (oco) <oco@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/8904e982605627d7b195fcb75f8899d535a0067c"
        },
        {
          "sha": "10f10176c3ce56c009c7eae953a617fc02569fc1",
          "author": {
            "email": "srma@odoo.com",
            "name": "Maira Salazar (srma)"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] hr_expense: show Create Report, Scan buttons in mobile\n\nCurrent behavior:\nIn hr_expenses, list and kanban views have different buttons being shown:\nlist view displays 'New', 'Scan' and 'Create Report', while kanban view\ndisplays only 'New' and 'Upload' (with same behavior as 'Scan'). In\nmobile, list view shows only 'New', and kanban shows 'Scan' and 'New'.\n\nExpected behavior:\n'Create Report' button should be displayed in both list and kanban view,\nin mobile or desktop. In mobile list view, 'Scan' should also be displayed.\nFor consistency between the kanban and list views (and also to match the\nbehavior of subsequent versions), button 'Scan' can be shown in mobile view,\nwhile 'Upload' can be displayed in desktok. This is more intuitive to the\nuser than can use a mobile device to scan receipts, and uploads an existing\nfile when on desktop.\n\nCause of the issue:\nThe static view for list includes only button 'Scan' with display utility\nclasses that hide the button in mobile. Similarly for 'Create Report'\nbutton in list. In Kanban, the button 'Create Report' has not been added.\n\nFix:\nIn the list view, 'Upload' button was added for desktop view, and the\nclasses of the 'Scan' button were changed to display it in mobile view.\nThe display utility classes for 'Create Report' were removed, so the\nbutton is displayed in mobile.\n\nIn kanban view, button 'Create Report' was added. When inheriting from\nweb.KanbanView.Buttons, the class 'align-items-baseline' is removed of\nthe control pannel buttons div and the alignment is instead done in its\nparent div. This ensures that the mobile view buttons are also displayed\ncorrectly. Without this change, the buttons 'New' and 'Scan' do not match\nthe height of mobile button 'Create Report'.\n\ntask-3981049\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#169396\n\nSigned-off-by: Olivier Colson (oco) <oco@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/10f10176c3ce56c009c7eae953a617fc02569fc1"
        },
        {
          "sha": "cc25b76a062a3a1a9b1e3cd4396064cf91b7352b",
          "author": {
            "email": "lost@odoo.com",
            "name": "Logan Staelens"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] l10n_nl: Merging migration script 3.2 and 3.3\n\nWith the version 3.3, the 3bl tax tag has been removed and so the 3.2 script is throwing an error since that tag doesn't exist anymore\n\nThe fix is that we remove the 3.2 script and change 3b tag to 3bg or 3bs in the 3.3 script along with the replacement of the 3bl tag\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#171737\n\nTask: 4032184\nSigned-off-by: Olivier Colson (oco) <oco@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/cc25b76a062a3a1a9b1e3cd4396064cf91b7352b"
        },
        {
          "sha": "b05ecf5d445dd93ba12f25694344d12feedf8a34",
          "author": {
            "email": "las@odoo.com",
            "name": "Laurent Smet"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] account: Fix 'percentage_st_line' on reco model\n\nThe current code is taking the residual amount instead of the statement line amount.\nWhen doing a reco model 'percentage_st_line' on 1000:\nLine 1 - 74%\nLine 2 - 24%\nLine 3 - 2%\n\nWe get:\n1000 * 0.74 = 740\n(1000 - 740) * 0.24 = 62.4\n(1000 - 740 - 62.4) * 0.02 = 3.95\n\nInstead of:\n1000 * 0.74 = 740\n1000 * 0.24 = 240\n1000 * 0.02 = 20\n\ntask_id: 3940370\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#166212\n\nRelated: odoo/enterprise#62884\nSigned-off-by: Claire Bretton (clbr) <clbr@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/b05ecf5d445dd93ba12f25694344d12feedf8a34"
        },
        {
          "sha": "4f071ecbe840828b02dd77dec7eb5ca897152512",
          "author": {
            "email": "quentin.dupont@grap.coop",
            "name": "Quentin Dupont"
          },
          "message": "[CLA] change for grap\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#171169\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Trigaux (mat) <mat@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/4f071ecbe840828b02dd77dec7eb5ca897152512"
