        {
          "sha": "561d67311273423f893198c486741c2c03b5046b",
          "author": {
            "email": "jmak@odoo.com",
            "name": "Joris Makauskis"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] base: stdnum library timeout\n\nstdnum library incorrectly sets zeep Transport timeout, resulting in\nsome requests hanging for 15 minutes. With this monkeypatch the timeout\nwill be set correctly.\nThe monkeypatch can be removed when\narthurdejong/python-stdnum/issues/444 is resolved and the version is\nupgraded\nRelated zeep github issue: mvantellingen/python-zeep#140\n\nopw-3980718\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#172080\n\nX-original-commit: 471c9753547dffa596ed4f689a39b7f52474a560\nSigned-off-by: Louis Baudoux (lba) <lba@odoo.com>\nSigned-off-by: Martin Trigaux (mat) <mat@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/561d67311273423f893198c486741c2c03b5046b"
        },
        {
          "sha": "1fbb47fbe8964b7c2fc1fd7e104fdefb93b3b264",
          "author": {
            "email": "jeas@odoo.com",
            "name": "jepbarasgarov"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] l10n_nl: fix syntax issue in `3.3` migration\n\nfixup for PR : #171737\n\nThis PR introduced syntax error while using `IN` with\n`sql.Literal` here[^1] and here[^2]. For fixing the issue I avoided\nusing `psycopg2` and used query parameters and cr.mogrify.\n\nsimilar traceback:\n```\n2024-07-09 13:20:03,873 5170 ERROR db_1790119 odoo.sql_db: bad query:\n                UPDATE account_account_tag_account_tax_repartition_line_rel\n                SET account_account_tag_id = 157\n                WHERE account_tax_repartition_line_id = ANY(ARRAY[59,60])\n                AND account_account_tag_id IN ARRAY[52]\n\nERROR: syntax error at or near \"ARRAY\"\nLINE 5:                 AND account_account_tag_id IN ARRAY[52]\n                                                      ^\n\n2024-07-09 13:20:03,880 5170 WARNING db_1790119 odoo.modules.loading: Transient module states were reset\n2024-07-09 13:20:03,881 5170 ERROR db_1790119 odoo.modules.registry: Failed to load registry\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/odoo/src/odoo/16.0/odoo/modules/registry.py\", line 90, in new\n    odoo.modules.load_modules(registry, force_demo, status, update_module)\n  File \"/home/odoo/src/odoo/16.0/odoo/modules/loading.py\", line 484, in load_modules\n    processed_modules += load_marked_modules(cr, graph,\n  File \"/home/odoo/src/odoo/16.0/odoo/modules/loading.py\", line 372, in load_marked_modules\n    loaded, processed = load_module_graph(\n  File \"/home/odoo/src/odoo/16.0/odoo/modules/loading.py\", line 236, in load_module_graph\n    migrations.migrate_module(package, 'post')\n  File \"/home/odoo/src/odoo/16.0/odoo/modules/migration.py\", line 189, in migrate_module\n    migrate(self.cr, installed_version)\n  File \"/home/odoo/src/odoo/16.0/addons/l10n_nl/migrations/3.3/post-migrate_update_taxes.py\", line 94, in migrate\n    cr.execute(\n  File \"/home/odoo/src/odoo/16.0/odoo/sql_db.py\", line 321, in execute\n    res = self._obj.execute(query, params)\npsycopg2.errors.SyntaxError: syntax error at or near \"ARRAY\"\nLINE 5:                 AND account_account_tag_id IN ARRAY[52]\n```\n\n[^1]: https://github.com/odoo/odoo/blob/16.0/addons/l10n_nl/migrations/3.3/post-migrate_update_taxes.py#L94-L104\n[^2]: https://github.com/odoo/odoo/blob/16.0/addons/l10n_nl/migrations/3.3/post-migrate_update_taxes.py#L64-L74\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#172515\n\nSigned-off-by: Claire Bretton (clbr) <clbr@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/1fbb47fbe8964b7c2fc1fd7e104fdefb93b3b264"
        },
        {
          "sha": "47cea4bc42259feb3f1b5ef232904306f258a3fd",
          "author": {
            "email": "tic@odoo.com",
            "name": "Tiffany Chang (tic)"
          },
          "message": "[I18N] hr_holiday: translate time off summary\n\nA few translation issues are fixed with this:\n- The title of the report was not translating the type of leave\n- The title was not correctly formatting the dates accroding to the\n  locale of the user.\n- The months were not translated\n- The days were not translated\n\nCleaning of the title's English will be done in master\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#172389\n\nX-original-commit: 9835632d8c193218d6705c630aa5c6e8db705312\nSigned-off-by: Tiffany Chang (tic) <tic@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/47cea4bc42259feb3f1b5ef232904306f258a3fd"
        },
        {
          "sha": "411a0edb914ce8f0c9d8e4db493b598789c42cb5",
          "author": {
            "email": "akim.juillerat@camptocamp.com",
            "name": "Akim Juillerat"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] account: Allow skipping bank account creation on reconciliation\n\nThis commit introduces system parameter to skip the creation of bank\naccount in the reconciliation of bank statements.\n\nThe issue it can solve happens when 2 different commercial entities\nuse the same paying partner (ie a partner that is not a subcontact)\nto pay their invoices.\n\nWhen an invoice is paid by the paying partner, Odoo will store the\naccount number that was used for the transfer on account.bank.statement.line.\nWhen this statement line is reconciled with an invoice, if the bank\naccount was not stored on the partner previously, a res.partner.bank will be\ncreated automatically.\nWhen another payment is coming from the same bank account, Odoo will\nthen select the partner linked to the bank account that it did store\npreviously, even if the payment was for an invoice linked to another partner,\nand it will not propose the proper invoice in the reconciliation widget,\neven if it uses an exact match on the payment reference number.\n\nHaving a parameter allowing to skip creation of the bank account in Odoo\nwill allow the reconciliation to be based striclty on the reference number.\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#169239\n\nX-original-commit: 62354663c6622f6d059e36097f0455ab5890b616\nSigned-off-by: Laurent Smet (las) <las@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/411a0edb914ce8f0c9d8e4db493b598789c42cb5"
        },
        {
          "sha": "dfc8bfdfc5c5c7db86a36088d4bede48154a7a04",
          "author": {
            "email": "yajo.sk8@gmail.com",
            "name": "Jairo Llopis"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] google_calendar: recurrence splitting\n\nImagine a scenario where Odoo and Google calendars are synced. Then, this happens:\n1. User goes to Google and changes one event from a recurrence series.\n2. When saving, user chooses to modify \"this event and all upcoming\".\n3. Odoo syncs from Google automatically via cron.\n\nIn such case, due to the way this was handled, Odoo would die with `MissingError`.\n\nHere I contribute a test for such scenario and the fix.\n\n@moduon MT-6287\n\nPart-of: odoo/odoo#172103\nSigned-off-by: Arnaud Joset (arj) <arj@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/dfc8bfdfc5c5c7db86a36088d4bede48154a7a04"
        },
        {
          "sha": "6cbd6b9f59f870b90c89ab69af1ce0d2d8ae6339",
          "author": {
            "email": "yajo.sk8@gmail.com",
            "name": "Jairo Llopis"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] google_calendar: avoid MissingError when cancelling already-removed events\n\nWhen a user re-schedules a recurring event, it can cause some events to be removed. In that case, they shouldn't be cancelled again in Odoo, as they don't exist anymore.\n\n@moduon MT-6287\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#172103\n\nSigned-off-by: Arnaud Joset (arj) <arj@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/6cbd6b9f59f870b90c89ab69af1ce0d2d8ae6339"
        },
        {
          "sha": "0ff6b4b81bd847ef2136e326a2d40c9e233c0eb9",
          "author": {
            "email": "pebr@odoo.com",
            "name": "Pedram (pebr)"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] pos_loyalty: ensure PoS opens when a program lacks rewards\n\nBefore this commit, the absence of rewards in a loyalty program would\ntrigger an error, preventing the Point of Sale from opening. Although\nthe current design does not support removing all rewards from a\nprogram, there exist databases in this state.\n\nopw-4045063\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#172597\n\nSigned-off-by: Joseph Caburnay (jcb) <jcb@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/0ff6b4b81bd847ef2136e326a2d40c9e233c0eb9"
        },
        {
          "sha": "25b7491d15a5e3249f0e6c649a37cbd75b5b3ae7",
          "author": {
            "email": "divy@odoo.com",
            "name": "divy-odoo"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] website: close navbar dropdown on page click\n\nIssue:\nIn edit mode, the \"on click\" dropdown remains open even after clicking\noutside of the dropdown.\n\nWith this pull request [1], we manually handle the dropdown to keep it\nopen when clicking a dropdown item, but it prevents the dropdown from\nclosing when clicking outside of the menu.\n\nBefore this commit, we only handled the on-page click event for the\nHoverableDropdown [2], but not for the clickable dropdown. To maintain\nthe same behavior for both clickable and hoverable dropdowns, this\ncommit binds the onPageClick event once we entered in edit mode.\n\n[1]: https://github.com/odoo/odoo/commit/fe67b34f1a03d838df82a1307cf6467f994a8f3b\n[2]: https://github.com/odoo/odoo/commit/455e03c743d6f1db70fab4e82b2fdbc963bc22ef\n\ntask-3370847\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#171507\n\nX-original-commit: 83be3ccceb605077544e0fb9cc4fbf7476f1d2f5\nSigned-off-by: Robin Lejeune (role) <role@odoo.com>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/beshoynabeih/odoo-dev/commits/25b7491d15a5e3249f0e6c649a37cbd75b5b3ae7"
        },
        {
          "sha": "949d9e769fc1f9ccbfd9b0e81515e36c24f628ee",
          "author": {
            "email": "wil@odoo.com",
            "name": "Louis Wicket (wil)"
          },
          "message": "[FIX] web: add utils_tests to the qunit_suite_tests bundle\n\nThe file utils_tests.js was not listed in the web.qunit_suite_tests\nassets bundle, preventing it from loading and rendering it useless.\n\nThis commit updates the assets bundle definition to properly load\nutils_tests.js.\n\ncloses odoo/odoo#172615\n\nX-original-commit: e8272ebba684a0af9c77417e03228f1c4c9b6817\nSigned-off-by: Tiffany Chang (tic) <tic@odoo.com>\nSigned-off-by: Louis Wicket (wil) <wil@odoo.com>",
