        "body": "[Just like Git for Windows v2.48.0-rc1](https://github.com/git-for-windows/git/pull/5337#issuecomment-2565876299), Due to `ps/build-sign-compare`, a couple of comparisons now need casts (and some loop variables need a different type).\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Range-diff relative to -rc0</summary>\r\n\r\n\r\n* 1:  e1ee1fb2a95 =   1:  d43df21d1a4 sparse-index.c: fix use of index hashes in expand_index\r\n* 3:  a487ef4f9f1 =   2:  ed3fe89027b t: remove advice from some tests\r\n* 4:  2273c7366ad =   3:  9a3602c684b t1092: add test for untracked files and directories\r\n* 2:  e4bf5baabd7 =   4:  d5da60b467a t5300: confirm failure of git index-pack when non-idx suffix requested\r\n* 5:  610b51f64d6 =   5:  f27fd55b79c index-pack: disable rev-index if index file has non .idx suffix\r\n* 16:  e9faa7ca313 =   6:  a83676d9c97 trace2: prefetch value of GIT_TRACE2_DST_DEBUG at startup\r\n* 6:  41e508aa7b3 !   7:  067993673df survey: calculate more stats on refs\r\n\r\n   ``````diff\r\n   @@ builtin/survey.c: static void survey_report_plaintext_refs(struct survey_context\r\n     \tclear_table(&table);\r\n     }\r\n    @@ builtin/survey.c: static void survey_phase_refs(struct survey_context *ctx)\r\n   - \tfor (size_t i = 0; i < ctx->ref_array.nr; i++) {\r\n   + \tfor (int i = 0; i < ctx->ref_array.nr; i++) {\r\n     \t\tunsigned long size;\r\n     \t\tstruct ref_array_item *item = ctx->ref_array.items[i];\r\n    +\t\tsize_t len = strlen(item->refname);\r\n   ``````\r\n\r\n* 7:  7c49aec1e70 !   8:  97b69001568 survey: show some commits/trees/blobs histograms\r\n\r\n   ``````diff\r\n   @@ builtin/survey.c: struct survey_report_ref_summary {\r\n    +\r\n    +static int hbin(unsigned long value)\r\n    +{\r\n   -+\tfor (int k = 0; k < HBIN_LEN; k++) {\r\n   ++\tfor (size_t k = 0; k < HBIN_LEN; k++) {\r\n    +\t\tif ((value & ~(HBIN_MASK)) == 0)\r\n    +\t\t\treturn k;\r\n    +\t\tvalue >>= HBIN_SHIFT;\r\n   @@ builtin/survey.c: struct survey_report_ref_summary {\r\